      "why": "Full pipelining gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax. At W=14-18 the datapath is short enough that Fmax should comfortably exceed 50 MHz, meeting the 50 MSPS constraint. This family is the cleanest 1/cycle option and its power scales with the number of registered stages (N), so it anchors the low-power end of the front for a given accuracy."
    }
  ,
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 14,
          "high": 20
        ,
