          "choices": ["trunc", "round"]
        },
        {
          "param": "m",
          "low": 2,
          "high": 4
        ,
          "choices": null
        }
      ],
      "budget_share": 0
    ,
      "why": "Registering every m stages cuts the flip-flop count (and hence power) versus full pipelining while still delivering 1 result/cycle, so it can dominate pipelined on power at equal accuracy. The longer combinational path (m rotations/cycle) risks Fmax < 50 MHz, so m is capped at 4 and the search will reveal the throughput/accuracy/power trade-off. This is where the interesting power-vs-accuracy trade-off lives."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec needs 50 MSPS, which only the 1-result/cycle families (pipelined, pipelined_m) can guarantee without depending on a high Fmax; iterative/unrolled_k are excluded by my assignment anyway. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) is met by n_iter ~ 12-14 with modest guards, so I bound n_iter to 12-18 and data_width to 14-20 to keep the datapath short (high Fmax, low power) while still reaching 12+ bits of accuracy. angle_guard is kept near 0 (the atan-LUT width barely needs to exceed W for this accuracy) and frac_guard is kept low (0-2) since extra fractional bits cost area/power without helping the 2^-12 target. Rounding is left to the search. I split the budget between the two families so the front captures both the full-pipeline baseline and the register-thinned (m>1) low-power variants, letting the hypervolume pick the best power/accuracy trade-off. The selection rule (min power_index) will then pick the lowest-power feasible point on that front."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established with 11 designs covering the trade-off space effectively. The minimum power_index achieved is 1.84 (pipelined_m, data_width=18, n_iter=15, m=3), which satisfies the throughput constraint (51.9 MSPS >= 50) and accuracy constraint (12.3 bits > 12). The front spans power_index 1.84 to 4.59 and accuracy_bits 12.3 to 14.6, providing a good spread for the hypervolume objective. Since this is the final round, further exploration is not possible. The selection rule (min power_index) picks the pipelined_m design with power_index=1.84, which is a valid, low-power solution meeting all constraints."
,
  "next_plan": null
}
